# Vendored third-party files must keep their upstream bytes EXACTLY.
#
# nimbus issue #495: schema/telemetry.schema.json is a pinned copy of a
# file this repo does not own, and tests/test_vendored_telemetry_schema.py
# asserts its sha256 against the upstream bytes. Without this line, git's
# own eol conversion rewrites LF to CRLF in a Windows working tree, the
# hash stops matching, and the drift check fails on a fresh clone while
# passing in Linux CI -- a break that would look like the schema had
# drifted when nothing had.
#
# `-text` disables eol conversion entirely for these paths, which is what
# byte-fidelity to an upstream source requires.
schema/** -text

# Golden-master snapshots are compared byte-for-byte against freshly
# regenerated bytes (tests/test_golden_snapshot_format.py), so they must keep
# LF endings in every working tree for exactly the reason given above.
#
# nimbus issue #1359 moved these from .json.gz to plain .json so a behaviour
# change shows up as a readable diff. Without this line, git's eol conversion
# would rewrite them to CRLF on Windows, the canonical-form check would fail
# on a fresh clone, and regenerating on Windows would show all 14 as modified.
tests/golden/snapshots/** -text
